        is strictly smaller than its enclosing loop's); the owner map is
        updated as instructions move, so an operand hoisted to a block
        outside the current body -- whether earlier in this loop's
        fixpoint sweep or while processing an inner loop -- reads as
        defined outside the loop.  Every instruction object moves once.
